    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 20,
        "data": {
          "text": "# OSC-driven visual\nDrive this patch from TouchDesigner, Max, Ableton or any OSC app: send UDP to this machine on port 9000. Without OSC it runs on its own LFO; each part switches to OSC as soon as its messages arrive.\n- 1. Terminal: npm run io-bridge (prints a token and a pairing URL)\n- 2. Output › I/O settings: paste the token, tick Enable I/O for this session\n- 3. Second terminal: npm run osc-demo (sends an LFO), or your app → 127.0.0.1:9000\n## Addresses\n- /patchtoy/lfo f · ring size and rotation\n- /patchtoy/xy f f · center (0..1)\n- /patchtoy/color f f f · tint (0..1 RGB)\n- /patchtoy/beat (any) · one flash per message\nOSC Out sends the flash back to 127.0.0.1:9001: allow it in Output › I/O to receive it in your app.",
          "width": 600,
          "height": 330,
          "color": "blue"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "type": "Comment",
        "x": 700,
        "y": 20,
        "data": {
          "text": "# OSC In → control\nEach OSC In holds its last message. Min(count, 1) is 0 until the first message, so Mix switches from the fallback (built-in LFO, center, orange) to OSC. Lag smooths the jumps; Envelope Follower turns /patchtoy/beat events into a decaying flash.",
          "width": 520,
          "height": 150,
          "color": "green"
        }
      },
